:: Story Stylesheet [stylesheet]
body {
  background-size: cover;
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
  background-attachment: fixed;
  transition: background-image 0.5s ease;
  .dialogue-box {
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 30px;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    
    width: 80%;
    max-width: 1000px;
    
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);
    color: white;
    
    padding: 25px 35px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    
    border: 2px solid #333;
    border-radius: 4px;
    
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    
    z-index: 100;
  }
  .character-name {
    color: #c9a86a;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
  }
  .character-layer {
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 10;
  }

  .character {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    max-height: 80vh;
    width: auto;
  }

  .katrina {
    bottom: 45%
  }
}

body.forest-bg {
  background-image: url("https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1491466424936-e304919aada7?fm=jpg&q=60&w=3000&auto=format&fit=crop&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8MTkyMHgxMDgwfGVufDB8fDB8fHww");
}

/* testing for different backgrounds, will use later */
body.desert-bg {
  background-image: url("https://media.istockphoto.com/id/968272302/vector/daytime-cartoon-flat-style-desert-landscape.jpg?s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=bXZoHX7RsebQn6i9KX17W7ix6PbRL-AKAKdPjWAkljU=");
}

:: Start [forest-bg]
<div class="dialogue-box">
  I've had many types stumble into my office.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S1]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S1 [desert-bg]
<div class="character-layer">
    <img class="character katrina" src="images/katrina.png">
</div>
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  Violent criminals. Beautiful dames.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S2]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S2
<div class="dialogue-box">
  Even those law enforcement types, who think flashing a badge makes them some sorta King. 
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S3]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S3
<div class="dialogue-box">
  Always asking me to find things.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S4]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S4
<div class="dialogue-box">
  Find the murderer.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S5]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S5
<div class="dialogue-box">
  Find their friend.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S6]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S6
<div class="dialogue-box">
  Find their goddamn stolen pearls.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S7]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S7
<div class="dialogue-box">
  I don’t mind that. The green flows in, and that's all that matters to me.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S8]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S8
<div class="dialogue-box">
  But there is one type that I really can’t stand. That personality that makes me wanna push a guy off a cliff.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S9]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S9
<div class="dialogue-box">
  God, I hate idiots.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S10]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S10
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // The scene reveals. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S11]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S11
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // You sit in your office. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S12]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S12
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // A man sits in front of you. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S13]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S13
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // In your left hand you hold a cigar. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S14]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S14
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // In your right hand is a black fountain pen. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S15]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S15
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // A blank legal pad lies on the desk in front of you. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S16]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S16
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // The rain beats softly against your windows. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S17]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S17
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // The blinds are drawn low. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S18]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S18
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // You sigh in frustration. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S19]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S19
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  Well? Say it, spit it out. Haven't got all day.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S20]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S20
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // The stranger who sits in front of you is peculiar to say the least. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S21]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S21
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // The blinds block the light and cover his face in shadow. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S22]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S22
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // You cannot identify any of his features. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S23]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S23
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // Something tells you he prefers it that way. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S24]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S24
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">???</div>
  Well, two weeks ago, I paid a man to kill me. Gave him a month. No day. No time.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S25]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S25
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  Which man?
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S26]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S26
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">???</div>
  ...My drug dealer.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S27]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S27
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // You scoff derisively. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S28]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S28
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  Not the fastest bullet in the barrel, are you?
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S29]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S29
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">???</div>
  Don't. It was a dark time for me, and I needed someone kind to do it. Dug was the kindest man I ever met.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S30]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S30
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  Huh. A kind drug dealer. That's new.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S31]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S31
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // The figure in front of you stiffens, agitated. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S32]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S32
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">???</div>
  A man like you would never understand. Sitting happily atop your ugly high horse.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S33]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S33
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">???</div>
  I wanted to drown. I wanted to end me. But then, I found what I needed.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S34]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S34
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  And what's that?
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S36]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S36
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">???</div>
  Hope.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S37]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S37
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  (Fantastic. Not only is he an idiot, he's a sentimental. That's even worse.)
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S38]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S38
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  That's sweet, pal. Really. But why're you here? What do you want from me?
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S39]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S39
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">???</div>
  I need you to find him. I need you to stop him.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S40]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S40
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  From killing you?
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S41]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S41
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">???</div>
  Yes.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S42]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S42
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // You chuckle dryly. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S43]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S43
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  What an odd job. I might have refused if you hadn't promised me such a pretty penny.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S44]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S44
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  Alright, stranger, I'll do it for you.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S45]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S45
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  But tell me one thing...what changed your mind? The world ain't a happy place.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S47]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S47
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  Why stay?
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S48]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S48
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">???</div>
  There was...a question I needed answered. I was lost. My life was empty.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S49]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S49 
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">???</div>
  But after I filled it with other things, my life became full again. I didn't need the answer anymore.
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S51]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S51
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  (Damn it. I hate a guy who talks in riddles. Shouldn't have asked him in the first place.)
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S52]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S52
<div class="dialogue-box">
  <div class="character-name">Detective Blackwell</div>
  But what was the question?
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S53]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S53
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // A few beams of light escape through the slits of the blinds... //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S54]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S54
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // Illuminating the lower half of the stranger's face for a split second. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S55]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S55
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // Perhaps you were imagining it but... //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S56]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S56
<div class="dialogue-box">
  // You thought you saw the glimpse of a smile. //
  <span class="next-button">
    [[Next|S57]]
  </span>
</div>

:: S57
???: Can a debt of blood...

[[Next|S58]]

:: S58
...truly be repaid?

[[Next|S59]]

:: S59
(add dues to pay title card here)

[[Next|P1]]

:: P1
// You stand in an office that is not your own.

[[Next|P2]]

:: P2
// It is hopelessly cluttered with case files and completely devoid of the cleanliness of your own office.

[[Next|P3]]

:: P3
// This, strangely, does not bother you however. 

[[Next|P4]]

:: P4
// Mostly due the cheery, spectacles-wearing middle aged man sitting at the disorganized desk in front of you.

[[Next|P5]]

:: P5
// His presence, extremely open and trusting, puts you at ease.

[[Next|P6]]

:: P6
// A naturally friendly creature, a true confidant.

[[Next|P7]]

:: P7
// You grin.

[[Next|P8]]

:: P8
You: Johnson, good to see you. Whatcha got for me?

[[Next|P9]]

:: P9
Johnson: Hey boss! We've tried finding the dealer but your client wasn't very helpful. His descriptions were vague and he refused to meet with a sketch artist.

[[Next|P10]]

:: P10
You: Yeah, Shadow Man's not the nicest company. Don't take it personally.

[[Next|P11]]

:: P11
Johnson: Shadow Man?

[[Next|P12]]

:: P12
You: Gave him a nickname. Makes him less intimidating.

[[Next|P13]]

:: P13
Johnson: I dunno, boss. He's still pretty scary.

[[Next|P14]]

:: P14
You: You're darn right, he gave me the shivers.

[[Next|P15]]

:: P15
Johnson: Anyways, we did find some possible contacts that would know about his whereabouts.

[[Next|P15.4]]

:: P15.4
// He hands you three case files, talking amiably as you flip through them.

[[Next|P16]]

:: P16
Katrina Kordoff - She owns that luxurious bar on South Street. She's a huge gossip and knows everyone's business. Rumor is she can charm anyone with those pretty eyes of hers. Be careful though! I heard she's a dangerous one.

[[Next|P17]]

:: P17
Jayl Sael - Most well known (and feared) crimunal this side of the city. An accomplished bounty hunter who can find anyone and everyone. He seems like a very shady fellow. Keeps to himself. But if you need to locate someone without any clues? He's your guy.

[[Next|P18]]

:: P18
Verie Newman - The newest junior officer on the force. Nice kid, bit a chatterbox though. Would probably be able to spill the beans on any recent criminal activity. If you talk to him, you're sure to get some good info that only the police could know. He's on a museum shift tonight, so maybe you can catch him for a chat!

[[Next|P19]]

:: P19
Johnson: So, which one are you gonna go after?

[[Katrina Kordoff| K1]]

[[Jayl Sael| J1]]

[[Verie Newman| V1]]

:: K1
// You lift Kordoff's file with interest. A bar, especially one favored by the city's criminals, is a hotspot of information, you think.

[[Next|K2]]

:: K2
// Johnson adjusts his glasses.

[[Next|K3]]

:: K3
Johnson: You sure, boss? Hearsay can only get you so far, not the most pragmatic option.

[[Next|K4]]

:: K4
You: Dunno. Maybe she's got gossip to uncover?? In my experience, a man is most sincere when he's drunk.

[[Next|K5]]

:: K5
Johnson: Boss, come on now. You hate alcohol.

[[Next|K6]]

:: K6
// You chuckle.

[[Next|K7]]

:: K7
You: Damn right, Johnson. But still, my gut's telling me it's worth a try.

[[Next|K8]]

:: K8
// Johnson grins excitedly.

[[Next|K9]]

:: K9
Johnson: Alright, then. Best of luck, Detective Blackwell!

[[Next|K10]]

:: K10
~

[[Next|K12]]

:: K12
// You stop to admire the outside of The Silk Shot, the sleek and modern bar that's been the talk of the town.

[[Next|K13]]

:: K13
// The neon lights catch your eyes, but it rattles your nerves for reasons you can’t seem explain.

[[Next|K14]]

:: K14
// You open the doOr, passing through the crowd of soft murmurs.

[[Next|K15]]

:: K15
// You approach the bar and absent-mindedly share your order with the bartender as your eyes inspect the customers in their booths.

[[Next|K16]]

:: K16
You: One gin.

[[Next|K17]]

:: K17
You: Say, you know if Katrina's around? Need a word.

[[Next|K18]]

:: K18
// The voice that answers you is not the rough grunt of a bartender.

[[Next|K19]]

:: K19
// It is smooth and feminine. Soft and alluring.


